Meet FamGenie: an AI assistant for busy parents.

It keeps an eye on the things that slip through the cracks: did they get to practice, which coach texted, who's asking you for money, and what's on the school calendar this week. It only speaks up when something needs you.

Free to start. {link}

Three kids, two schools, a tutor, a coach and a parents' group chat. Sound familiar?

With FamGenie they all text one family number, and you see every message in one place. Anyone you haven't approved waits quietly instead of buzzing your phone.

{link}

"Mom, I need $40 for the tutor." Now it's one text.

Your kid asks, you approve, and you pay in your own Venmo, Zelle or PayPal. FamGenie never touches the money; it keeps the tally so you can see what each kid spent this month.

{link}

Hi everyone, a bit of a different post. I built a small app for our own family's chaos and the admins said it was OK to share.

It's called FamGenie. Kids can check in with one tap (no tracking app on their phone), coaches and tutors text one family number so it's all in one inbox, and kids can ask for money that you approve and pay in Venmo or Zelle.

It's free to start. I'm genuinely looking for honest feedback from other parents, good or bad: {link}
